  "texts": {
    "preamble": "C.J.Francis vs Food Safety Officer on 22 November, 2018 Author: K.Abraham Mathew Bench: K.Abraham Mathew In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice K.Abraham Mathew Thursday, The 22Nd Day Of November 2018 / 1St Agrahayana, 1940 Crl.MC.No. 7874 of 2018 Against Cc 787/2018 of J.M.F.C., Kodungalloor Petitioner: C.J.Francis, Aged 52 Years S/O. Joseph, Residing At Chakkalakkal House, Kottappuram P.O., Kodungalloor, Thrissur District, Pin - 680 667. By Advs. Sri.Santhosh Subramanian Sri.E.A.Thankappan Sri.Sherry J. Thomas Sri.S.Sreekumar(North Paravur) Respondents: 1 Food Safety Officer, Kodungalloor Circle, Kodungalloor, Pin - 680 664. 2 State Of Kerala Represented By Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam,Pin-682031.",
    "facts": "The petitioner was the first accused in C.C.No. 2493 of 2016 on the file of the Judicial Magistrate of First Class, Kodungalloor. He along with the co-accused allegedly committed certain offences under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. This court by Annexure III order [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the co-accused on the ground that the Director of Food Regulatory Complaints Division directed all States and Union Territories not to launch prosecutions for non-conformance of limit of iron filings in cases where samples were picked up/tested prior to 19/05/2016. They were also advised to withdraw all such prosecutions launched prior to 19/05/2016. The proceedings against the petitioner are now pending as C.C.No. 787 of 2018.",
